# Finite coordinates for the binary Ree incidence graph

The first 1755 labels are point cosets and the last 2925 labels are line
cosets. Incidence is membership in the recorded three-point line rows;
there are no edges within a type. The packed rows were discovered from the
37 Parrott relators with the original endpoint generators. The separate
model comparison proves that these coordinates are the literal Ree cosets;
this definition assumes no group-action or automorphism conclusion.

Point rows agree with the existing certified R1-coset numbering. Discovery
and immutable adjacency data are recorded with the automorphism certificate.
